{
  "case_id": "2001-00-973",
  "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent pleaded guilty with counsel by his side after having been advised at least twice earlier in the proceedings of his right to the assistance of counsel at all stages of the proceedings. The court of appeals, nevertheless, set aside his guilty plea on the ground that the district court, during the guilty plea colloquy, had failed to advise respondent of his right to the assistance of counsel as required by rule 11(c)(3) of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure. The court of appeals decision is wrong for three reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Souter, I believe that the reason that the drafters picked just one is that the drafters were addressing a specific holding of this Court that, as Justice O'Connor indicated, had suggested that there was automatic reversal in the case of a rule 11 violation. And the drafters wanted to negate that specific holding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But the cleanest way to negate it would be to simply say, you engage in some kind of an analysis of consequences. You either do it in terms of -- of harmless error or you do it in in terms of plain error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You could. I believe that there's a general presumption in the Federal criminal system that if an error is preserved at trial, it's subject to harmless error review, which is what rule 11(h) provides for. If an error is not preserved at trial, it's subject to review only under the plain error rule, rule 52(b), and this --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That -- that rule is a response to this Court's decision in Boykin v. Alabama which held that if the record is entirely silent on whether the defendant entered a knowing and intelligent plea, a court of appeals on direct review cannot uphold it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: This isn't much of a sanction on the judge anyway. He's not the prosecutor. He's not supposed to care whether this guy gets convicted or not, is he?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: The burden of proof you're talking about then is not actually an evidentiary burden. It's the burden that the court of appeals judges the case by."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: This is not a minor deviation. This is not a minor deviation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "advisory committee added (g) to the rule, to say that specifically."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Knox",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Other than the policy reason that we've discussed, as well as what my argument as to what the advisory committee meant when it put both (g)and (h) into the rule, I don't have another reason that the Court should do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Knox",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the Court itself recognized in Hyde that all provisions of the rules are not the same in the (c) and (d) provisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defendant",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He specifically denied that either he personally had a gun or that he had any knowledge of his co-defendants having guns."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-973",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d7b378961710d3d58b265728a75ec831994cd9964f36d24fe9784560ac50779",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d7b37896171-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
